# Nothing a person types is installed on a child's computer: labwc suggests
# a terminal, Chromium, for the web applications, has one among its
# recommendations, and wmenu is a launcher's menu; the virtual package is
# every terminal emulator there is.
Conflicts: foot,
           wmenu,
           x-terminal-emulator,
Description: Kidux sessions: the kiosk, the lock screen, and every door closed
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. This package makes
 the machine boot into the Kidux sign-in screen and nothing else, runs each
 child's session with the Kidux launcher and the learning modules an adult
 has enabled, gives the lock screen a screen of its own, and closes every
 way out of that: spare terminals, text logins, Ctrl+Alt+Delete, the SysRq
 keys, SSH for children, and the boot loader's editor.
 .
 Removing it turns the machine back into an ordinary Debian system at the
 next boot. Install it only on a machine set aside for a child.
